# k10t1 — the Harvey-kernel tier-1 venue config (06-09, G-06-1).
#
# Maintainer direction 2026-11-05 (06-UAT.md): on amd64/x86_64 the tier
# donor evidence comes from Harvey's OWN kernel, not 9front.  This config
# boots STANDALONE under plain qemu-system-x86_64 (D-03: no minimega, no
# network, no srv9, no 9front tree) with the amd64 tier-1 read-only set
# plus the D-10 sweep embedded in devroot, and runs the sweep from the
# embedded root at boot (the k10root standalone-boot shape: an rc script
# IS /boot/boot — initcode.c:26-29's "could be a shell script" contract).
#
# The device/dbgflg/mach/port/dir/lib sections are k10cpu's set VERBATIM
# (the poolpanic leg proved this exact set boots past the v1.0 pool
# panic) — DO NOT PRUNE: changing the device set risks new breakage for
# zero venue benefit.  The deliberate deltas vs k10cpu are ONLY:
#   rootdir — the 43-entry venue embed set below (35 swept h* binaries
#             + rc/echo/bind/rcmain + the boot script + 5 staged files;
#             devroot.c's Nbootfiles is raised 32 -> 64 for this).
#             NOTE: rc and echo embed under TWO names each (hrc+rc,
#             hecho+echo — the sweep's $B/h* vocabulary plus the boot
#             chain's bare-name resolution).  parse keys each entry's C
#             symbol name off the SOURCE path, so the second name rides
#             a staged copy (.tier1-stage/rc, .tier1-stage/echo) — the
#             same source twice would duplicate _amd64_bin_rc{code,len}
#             / _amd64_bin_echo{code,len} and 6l fails with 'multiple
#             initialization' (measured 2026-11-05, first venue build).
#   conf    — k10root's proven-compiling `int cpuserver = 1;` line
#             (semantically inert without boot.c).
# The boot section keeps k10cpu's `boot cpu` / `tcp` pair verbatim (it
# only feeds the boot$CONF.out rule, which nothing in this venue builds;
# k10root carries the same lines with an rc script as /boot/boot).

